  "hypothesis": "Drawbridge wall_info and subsequent door doormask diverge because C aliases the same flags word while JS stores separate fields.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Closed portcullis painted as ordinary door retains mask8; open-bridge ordinary doors have0 and secret replacements have4.",
  "observedBehavior": "Four targets: Cdoor mask8 versus JS0, with matching before-state. Eight open/secret controls match. Former bridge span is repainted floor on both sides.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "production_api",
    "scope": "JS public level_init/terrain/drawbridge construction versus exact C wrappers and writers with checked typed readers/default-coordinate adapter; four directional targets and eight controls.",
    "limitations": [
      "Construction-only API sequence: default frame1,0, floor solidfill, explicit MOAT span14,10 and HWALL adjacent in each cardinal direction, explicit open/closed drawbridge, ordinary/secret door paint, then replace span with floor. Final fixture has no remaining drawbridge; no bridge/door operations, entities, object effects or gameplay commands execute.",
      "C executes exact lspo_level_init, lspo_drawbridge and lspo_terrain wrappers and exact construction/terrain writers. Typed table readers accept only the fixed supplied enum/integer inputs; coordinate adapter asserts default frame1,0, nonrandom interior coordinates and no room. This is not a full Lua VM or parser/coercion test.",
      "C rm.h aliases doormask/wall_info/drawbridgemask to flags. Minimal fixed structs preserve the used fields; coordinates are small in-range integers. Unused selection/parser and runtime-effect adapters abort if reached; exact is_ice executes, with no ice-removal path.",
      "Observed portcullis terrain, wall_info and orientation agree before painting. Four targets compare resulting ordinary-door type/mask/orientation. Eight controls cover initially-open bridges and secret-door replacement; they do not prove arbitrary bridge topology, metadata or runtime parity.",
      "Related to existing shared terrain-flag alias cases, but retention across drawbridge-to-door construction differs from earlier clearing/reset paths. Main must deduplicate repair identity; no additional independent-root or score-impact claim. Shipped exposure unknown."
    ]
